# STAGED — our own observations, SparkPNT SXT-D (mosaic-T) on UFO1, for Onocoy.
#
# Addressed BY NAME, deliberately.  This was hardcoded to 10.168.13.196, a
# dynamic DHCP lease; the box moved to a static address 2026-08-25 and the
# literal IP went dead.  str2str would have retried a dead address forever and
# the Onocoy feed would have gone SILENTLY off the air.
#
# The mosaic-T is a timing SKU (dgnssbase=0, rtkbase=0) and cannot emit RTCM3
# natively, so we transcode its SBF MeasEpoch.  1006/1033 are synthesised from
# OUR surveyed UFO1 ARP and antenna via -px/-a, independent of the receiver's
# own auto-survey and Unknown-antenna state.  This hop is the permanent steady
# state for this receiver, not a stage to retire.
#
# No CRED: the source is raw TCP on the LAN, unauthenticated.
#
# TO ACTIVATE, append the Onocoy push to ARGS and enable the instance:
#     -out ntrips://${ONOCOY_USER}:${ONOCOY_PASS}@servers.onocoy.com:2101/UFO1_MSM7#rtcm3
# Preconditions first — see onocoy-activation-README.md.  Note the wrapper does
# NOT expand ${VAR} inside ARGS; add the credential the same way IN does it, or
# put the literal push URL here.
#
# Shell-sourced by str2str-relay-exec (NOT a systemd EnvironmentFile), so
# ARGS must be QUOTED and $HOME expands.  '%Y%m%d_%h' is str2str's filename
# template and passes through untouched -- single %, no systemd escaping.
IN=tcpcli://sxt-d.VanValzah.Com:28800#sbf
ARGS="-msg 1077(1),1087(1),1097(1),1127(1),1006(10),1033(10),1230(10) -out ntripc://:2104/UFO1_MSM7#rtcm3 -out file://$HOME/opt/ntrip-relay/logs/prod/ufo1_msm7_%Y%m%d_%h.rtcm3::T::S=24 -px 157469.2017 -4756188.1927 4232767.8802 -a SFESPK6618H,NONE -i mosaic-T,GNSSDO+ -r 10000"

